Ambassador Jennifer Locetta
Alternative Representative for Special Political Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. And thank you to our briefers today.
The United States remains concerned by recent events in southeastern Yemen. We urge restraint and continued diplomacy to seek a lasting solution. We remain supportive of all efforts to advance our shared security interests.
We continue to support the Republic of Yemen Government and the Presidential Leadership Council to enhance Yemen’s security and stability.
We look to regional partners to support a Yemeni government that is united in purpose to counter the Houthi terrorists and the threat they pose to regional security and freedom of navigation.
The continued Houthi detention of staff of the UN, civil society organizations, and diplomatic missions, including the U.S. mission, exemplify the continued terrorist threat the Houthis pose. We condemn these detentions and the sham trials launched for some of the detainees. Once again, we call on the Houthis to immediately and unconditionally release all these detainees.
This Council must also act to counter the Houthi threat by depriving them of resources for their terrorist activities. We urge UN Member States follow the United States’ lead and designate and sanction the Houthis as a terrorist organization.
Finally, all Member States have an obligation to implement UN sanctions. Iran and others continue to defy this Council’s resolutions by supplying the Houthis with arms and related materiel, as well as with military, logistical, and intelligence support. These actions should carry consequences, including designation in the Yemen Sanctions Committee of those who fail to fully implement UN sanctions on the Houthis and their allies.
The United States strongly supports UN mechanisms that restrict the resources fueling Houthi terrorist activities, especially the UN Verification and Inspection Mechanism. Conversely, the UN Mission to Support the Hudaydah Agreement, UNMHA, has failed to gain traction in the face of Houthi obstructionism. We urge Council Members to support sunsetting the mission at the end of the month.
Thank you.
